	"descriptionMarkdown": "It's just more Ethical™\n\n- Minimal fish killed (qual ladder, not washing)\n- Minimally habitat-invasive (keeps fish fresh with minimal re-breeds)\n- Natural (zero non-const combinators, zero timers)\n\nNeeds ~18 fish breeds per qual tier (~6% upgrade, ~19% recycle, +1.5 fish per breed). \\\n**ETA to leg is 3h** (w/ high variance):\n-> uncom: 5m -> rare: +15m -> epic: +40m -> leg: +2h\n\nAfter reaching legendary, keeps a 4-fish stock fresh by comparing against biter egg spoil times with inserter 'spoiled-first'. Since the latter is a time-remaining check not a %-check, fish are refreshed only once they're < 30m from spoiling.\n\nUSAGE:\n\n- Put any qual pair of fish in the wagon\n- To change the ready-fish stock count (default 4), update the buffer chest cap, plus the adjacent steel chest's outserter.\n\nLogistically supply:\n- Spawner bioflux (1/m)\n- Legendary spoilage: \\\n   If you didn't change the default stock count (4), the life support and a surplus of\n   **~1 fish / hour** should be **self-sufficient** from its ~5/m built-in leg. spoilage production. \\\n   If you raised the stock amount or use fish faster, needs ~1/m leg spoilage per stocked fish (of which ~5/m is self-provided),\n   plus ~300 per consumed fish.\n\nNote: Finishes gambling away lower-qual fish pairs before starting next qual; this is expected.\n\nNote: Currently affected by https://forums.factorio.com/viewtopic.php?t=136478; unstick stack inserter if it looks stuck.\n\n[v1.6] Changed stock amount to be self-sufficient by default.",
